// @exit 12
// @stdout alpha says one
// @stdout beta says one two
// Two sibling modules each define a `private helper` (same shape) and a `private describe`
// (different parameter counts). Both keep internal linkage, so the emitted objects link
// cleanly, and each symbol is qualified by its module, so the cross-function passes never
// merge two same-named private functions' facts. Every public wrapper calls its own module's
// private function; the distinct results confirm each call stays inside its module.
import alpha;
import beta;

main() -> int {
    print(alpha.sayAlpha("one"));
    print(beta.sayBeta("one", "two"));
    return (alpha.wrapperAlpha() + beta.wrapperBeta()) as int;
}
